s", 58.887, 59.256], ["final", 59.256, 59.626], ["boss", 59.626, 60.041], ["hers", 60.24, 60.432], ["says", 60.432, 60.794], ["his", 60.94, 61.163], ["boss", 61.163, 61.563], ["her", 61.778, 61.893], ["red", 61.893, 62.078], ["bar", 62.078, 62.332], ["doesn't", 62.332, 62.539], ["fit", 62.539, 62.755], ["in", 62.755, 62.801], ["the", 62.801, 62.87], ["town", 62.87, 63.409]], "lines": [[0.062, 7.201, "In this town, the priest reads every kid their class. Fighter. Mage. Thief. He read mine, and dropped the book. Final Boss."], [7.438, 10.07, "A red bar appeared over my head. It was longer than our street."], [10.29, 12.628, "And in this town, heroes get paid to clear bosses."], [12.824, 15.14, "By lunch, four hundred of them were outside our bakery."], [15.303, 18.172, "Everyone thought I'd fight. I took a nap. On the front step."], [18.386, 20.989, "They hit me for an hour. I woke up once, to turn over."], [21.206, 24.108, "Then I stayed sitting, and started charging. Two coppers a swing."], [24.256, 26.14, "By sundown, I'd bought the bakery next door."], [26.338, 29.486, "The king doubled the reward. So I turned myself in, and collected it."], [29.654, 32.769, "The next day, I turned myself in again. He paid twice before he noticed."], [32.923, 36.076, "So he sent his dragon. It looked at my red bar, and asked for an apron."], [36.269, 38.684, "Then one hero gave up on me, and looked at my mom."], [38.895, 40.881, "I stood up. For the first time all week."], [41.037, 42.845, "The street cracked from our door to the castle."], [43.038, 44.007, "He's on dishes now."], [44.203, 47.824, "Finally the king came himself, with his biggest sword. I asked him to hold the door."], [47.972, 48.811, "He's still holding it."], [49.01, 54.524, "So that's who works at my mom's bakery. Four hundred heroes, a dragon, and a king. The bread is very safe."], [54.725, 58.452, "But today, my little sister had her turn. The priest read hers, and fainted."], [58.656, 61.563, "Mine says Final Boss. Hers says: His Boss."], [61.778, 63.409, "Her red bar doesn't fit in the town."]]}